2026-09-01T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Bao is the secret store, cert-auth is the fence
 # uuid: 5cb3922a-9291-5d20-9230-f81f819c8373
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:attest-in:details
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-09-01T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2146) 'the workspace's Bao instance and every consumer that already presents a per-identity TLS leaf.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2146) 'A service's TLS certificate is its login to Bao, with no shared bearer in between.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Every service ends up with three identity questions: what secrets can it read, what actions can it take, and how does it prove it is what it claims to be. Left alone, each answer accretes its own credential: a shared bearer for reads, a root token for writes, a network ACL as an identity substitute.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Check a new service against the rule above: one policy, one role, an exact-match CN with no globs. The sections below hold the role table.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Bao is the secret store, cert-auth is the fence
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2146) 'The cert is the answer. Bao's cert auth backend accepts each identity's per-service leaf as the login credential, mints a scoped token bound to that identity's role's policies, and returns it. No shared bearers, no root token in service code, no network ACL as an identity substitute. The cert is already the fence at TLS; this RFD extends it up the stack.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2146) 'The store becomes the source of truth for every secret; 1P retains the material as an offline mirror. Role table, walkthrough, negative controls in `DETAILS.md`.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2146) 'RFD66606-2140, RFD66606-2142 (implemented here), 2144, 2145.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2146) 'The two axes
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Two axes carry the design. **Policies** shape `<verb>-<scope>`: verb in {read, write, admin, issue}; scope is a KV subtree, a PKI mount, or `*` for sudo. **Roles** bind one identity's leaf (or a small exact-match CN allow-list, no globs) to a set of policies with a short-session TTL. New app: one policy, one role. New capability: one policy against an existing scope.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2146) 'KV layout
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Every secret under `secret/weftspun/*` is a source-of-truth entry tagged `{source_of_truth:true, moved_from:<1P item>, moved_at:<date>}`. 1P retains the same values as an offline mirror, so a Bao outage does not lock the operator out.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2146) '    secret/weftspun/fdb/cluster-id            weft:<hex>@<coord-list>
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2146) '    secret/weftspun/fdb/r2-dr                 R2 S3 keys (RFD 2143 fan-out)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2146) '    secret/weftspun/cloudflare/edit-zone-dns  bearer for chibifire.com zone DNS
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2146) '    secret/weftspun/cloudflare/r2-bearer      bearer for R2 bucket mgmt
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2146) 'App-scoped secrets go under `secret/apps/<app>/*` (empty today; roles below already fence access).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Policies
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Five policies, named for what they let you do, not who they're for.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2146) '    admin              path "*"                             sudo + all verbs
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2146) '    dns-editor         secret/{data,metadata}/weftspun/cloudflare/*   read, list
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2146) '    fdb-config-reader  secret/{data,metadata}/weftspun/fdb/*          read, list
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2146) '    pki-issuer         pki/issue/*, pki/sign/*,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2146) '                       pki-wt/issue/*, pki-wt/sign/*        create, update
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2146) '    app-reader-spot    secret/{data,metadata}/apps/spot-broker/*      read, list
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Naming convention: each policy is a verb ("editor", "reader", "issuer") over a scope ("dns", "fdb-config", "app-<name>"). Scopes map to KV subtrees; verbs to Bao capability sets.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Adding a new app is a policy per app (`app-reader-<name>`) plus one subtree under `secret/apps/<name>/*`. Adding a new capability is a policy per verb, per scope. Two axes; nothing else needs to change.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Cert-auth roles
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Bao's `cert` auth backend was enabled by RFD66606-2146. Every role binds one leaf (or a small allow-list of CNs) to a set of policies. The leaf is Bao-PKI-issued by `chibifire.com Intermediate CA v2` (except the operator's admin cert, which is signed directly by the Root, a one-hop shortcut that lets the admin swap in without an intermediate in the trust chain).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2146) '    role                cn(s)                                            policies
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2146) '    ---------------     ----------------------------------------------   ----------------------------------------
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2146) '    admin-v2            bao-admin.chibifire.com                          admin, dns-editor, pki-issuer,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2146) '                                                                         fdb-config-reader
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2146) '    spot-broker-app     fdb-spot-broker.chibifire.com                    fdb-config-reader, app-reader-spot
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2146) '    fdb-cluster         fdb-{8d1d2ebed71158,2861e4dc350678,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2146) '                            0803267bd16708}.chibifire.com                fdb-config-reader
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2146) '`allowed_common_names` is exact-match (no globs) so a compromised leaf under a shared CA cannot cross into another role's scope by renaming its CSR. Token TTL 8h, max TTL 24h, a session's window, not a service's lifetime.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

