2026-09-01T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2146) 'No `op read` in the chain. The admin cert is on this desk. Bao's cert-auth backend checks the presented leaf against the role, mints a scoped token, and returns it. Verified 2026-09-01 against `spot.chibifire.com` DNS records under the Cloudflare zone.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Negative controls (proved on the same day)
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2146) '- `spot-broker-app` logging in with its own cert reads `secret/data/weftspun/fdb/cluster-id` -> value returned; reads `secret/data/weftspun/cloudflare/edit-zone-dns` -> **permission denied**. The `app-reader-spot` + `fdb-config-reader` bundle has no path into `cloudflare/*`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2146) '- `fdb-cluster` logging in with an FDB machine cert reads `cluster-id` -> value returned; reads `cloudflare/edit-zone-dns` -> **permission denied**. `fdb-config-reader` is the only grant.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Both negative controls fire on the same DENIED shape a real attacker would see: 403 with `permission denied`. Nothing about the policy leaks to the caller.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2146) 'What this RFD does not cover
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2146) '- **Approle / token-based auth.** Kept enabled for the root break- glass path. Not the primary auth pattern for services.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2146) '- **Cert renewal.** Roles carry a specific leaf's DER hash. When the leaf rotates (90 days per RFD66606-2145), the role has to be re-bound. A followup script watches `pki/` for issuance and re-runs `bao write auth/cert/certs/<role> certificate=@<new-leaf>` automatically. Filed in the workspace task list.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2146) '- **Namespaces.** OpenBao has enterprise-only namespaces. This RFD uses path prefixes instead (`secret/weftspun/`, `secret/apps/`).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Sources
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2146) '- RFD66606-2140 (Bao on FDB), the storage backend this all sits on.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2146) '- RFD66606-2142, service TLS design; this RFD's role table is its implementation.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2146) '- RFD66606-2145, cert lifetimes that constrain how often roles rotate.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2146) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-01T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2146) 'Every one becomes a rotation problem and a leak surface. When the store sits behind mTLS, the client already presents a per-identity cert at the TLS handshake, and the API layer above ignores it and re-asks with a token.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2146  1 LINE
 Text:Written

